    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today with a clear emphasis on aggressive base-running and high-floor matchup exploitation. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.96) is our premier play, capitalizing on a lead-off spot against a soft matchup in a park that rewards his dynamic speed profile, even with a slight drag from wind conditions. He is joined at the top of our lineup logic by **Kazuma Okamoto** (69.87) and **Yordan Alvarez** (69.38), both of whom benefit from favorable park factors and high-impact lineup positioning. Despite a high-velocity threat on the mound, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (68.40) provides surprising depth at the UTIL spot, as his matchup against Scherzer presents a prime opportunity for power production given the favorable SP_xERA and park alignment.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages remain central to our daily construction, particularly with **Dillon Dingler** (63.90) and **Josh Smith** (62.54), who both receive significant boosts from defensive weaknesses in their respective matchups. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Trea Turner** (48.28); while he is a staple of our pursuit of stolen bases, his score is suppressed today by an elite opposing arm in Logan Henderson and a 40% strike-em-out-throw-em-out risk factor. Our most difficult personnel decision was benching **Chase Meidroth** (49.29), who hovered near the threshold of viability but ultimately lost out due to the high volume of better-projected outfield and middle-infield options. \n\nRisk management for this slate is centered on the \"Lineup Pending\" status of several starters, including **Gary Sanchez** and **Christian Yelich**, both of whom are facing Nola. While **Yelich** remains a strong play (61.65) due to his platoon edge, the wind blowing in could dampen the power output for both him and **Gary Sanchez** (46.61). We have verified that **Colt Keith**, **Casey Schmitt**, and **Jacob Gonzalez** remain unavailable, ensuring our focus remains strictly on the active roster. We continue to monitor the development paths of **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** as we balance immediate Roto category needs with long-term roster flexibility.",
